think The round-open named parked work -- tools/r/rye_build_witness.rish stood in stash@{0} and on no ref -- so this lap picked up the lap before it rather than opening anything new.
think The claim board still carried copal-rye-build-witness as mine and building, which is the board doing its job: the work was in flight and said so.
think A stale hot roster pass held the run lock at a launch_head four commits behind, its verdict already fixed at tree_moved; TERM released it per the runner's own instruction, and the process resolved to this tree before the signal.
think Popping the stash conflicted on tools/fixtures/r/rye_build_control.sh, because 10fcae2878 had widened that same control upstream while the parked lap was building its witness.
think Both sides were real readings, so both were kept rather than either chosen -- the trap now clears four lock directories, and the mutation's emitted binary moved off the room bound's name so two legs cannot share a path.
think The index had to come from HEAD rather than from the stash: fcba7af635 corrected nine composed stamps, and the stashed rows pointed at seven filenames that do not exist on disk.
obs The red this closes is exactly as old as the widening -- five cross-room legs landed unrun beside the ten already unrun, which is what an unheard control costs per lap rather than once.
obs A witness asserting only the control's verdict proves the control reached its last line, so all sixteen legs are asserted by name beside faults=0 and the total is counted off the leg lines rather than recited.
obs Three living pages recited the elder ten-and-eleven counts -- the roster comment, the ledger row, and the card -- and each was corrected against the control's own legs= line rather than against the others.
obs The hot pass reddened prose_register on a peer's page seated two hours earlier at 36 percent; two sentences carry the same claims affirmatively and the reading sits at its ceiling of 9.
obs The hot pass died at guard 246 on No space left on device; nineteen tools/am witnesses open a mktemp pen and none removes it, so the leak is on the success path and scales with healthy laps.
obs Reclaiming every pen untouched for three hours took /tmp from 94G to 11G and free space from 1.1G to 84G; the three-hour floor rather than a blanket wipe, because a peer's witness may be in flight.
obs A peer measured the same pier 107 seconds after that reclaim and wrote that 82G returned and nothing recorded it; naming the hand on their row is what a passing lane owes.
obs amphora_mark_wreck_witness.rish claims in its header that it WIPES its pen and carries no rm in 177 lines, which is the same fault as a proof nothing runs, one file over.
obs fixture_depth reds at HEAD on a peer's link_text_promise_scan.sh, whose pen plants no rishi/bin, so the sanctioned root walk would exit 2 inside it; reported rather than taken, since the repair moves that ship's pen layout.
obs The aether row's own pages had this lap's sentence already written: the Lindy foundation records a front-door claim that stood broken eighteen days and nothing could hear it.
